  "chain": "unresolved dual failure [cause X] -> motor surge/phase-to-phase fault -> Heater Drain Pump B trips on overcurrent -> motor fire; [in parallel] differential relay found tripped (cause undetermined) -> lockout relay trips -> Condensate Pump A fails to start -> lowering Main Feed suction pressure/SG levels -> manual reactor trip [backups AFW, Steam Dumps to Condenser]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel, independently-caused equipment failures (Heater Drain Pump B motor fault and Condensate Pump A differential relay malfunction) combined to cause the trip; both failure origins are captured as separate FailureMode nodes each CAUSED_BY the single official Cause node (code X / Other), since the licensee could not determine root cause for the relay and attributed the pump failure to an electrical surge rather than a specific personnel/design/equipment category. No previous similar events reported. Heater Drain and Condensate systems are non-safety-related per narrative; RPS and AFW actuated as designed as mitigation, not as pre-existing inoperable SSCs."
